== -E completes an empty line:
empty_one
empty_two
== -I completes the command word:
initial_one
initial_two
== -I completes the command word after a separator and an assignment:
initial_two
== -I leaves an argument alone:
slot_file
== -I with no match offers nothing:
== -I -o bashdefault with no match falls back to command names:
compopt
== the -E and -I functions receive the bash slot names:
[_EmptycmD_][][]
from_function
[_InitialWorD_][ab][ab]
from_function
== -D lists its actions:
slot_dir/
== -D lists its word list with the prefix:
pre_alpha
== a -D loader returning 124 restarts with the loaded spec:
loaded_one
loaded_two
== complete -r removes a named spec:
slot_file
== complete -r removes one slot:
complete -W 'w' cmd
complete -W 'i' -I
status 1
== complete -r with no name removes every spec:
status 0
== complete -r reports a missing spec and a missing slot:
status 1
status 1
== -D wins over -E, and -E over -I:
complete -W 'd' -D
complete -W 'e' -E
== complete -p prints the slots and round-trips:
complete -o nospace -c -I
complete -o default -F load -D
complete -W 'e1 e2' -E
complete -W 'e1 e2' -E
complete -W 'e1 e2' -E
round-trip-ok
== complete -p on a missing slot fails:
status 1
